==================================================
11A) WHY THE ADDED .JS FILES WERE NEEDED
==================================================
- js/time-display.js:
	I added this because I had the same clock logic appearing across multiple pages.
	Putting it into one shared file made updates quicker and kept the time/date behavior consistent everywhere.

- js/toast.js:
	I added this to remove repeated notification code in different pages.
	It gave me one reusable notification pattern and stopped small style/behavior differences from creeping in.

- js/shared-nav.js (expanded role):
	This file already existed, but I extended it to manage the shared interactions in one place (theme, profile photo upload/remove/persistence, and common nav behavior).
	From a development point of view, this made the project easier to maintain and reduced bugs caused by duplicate page-level scripts.

High-impact updated files:
- js/shared-nav.js
- css/shared-nav.css
- dashboard.html
- add-Assignment.html
- overview.html
- About.html
- css/dashboard.css

